  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-154786",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $x\\in (-\\infty ,-7)$ means that $x$ lies between $-\\infty $ and $-7,$ where \n\n- the left endpoint $-\\infty $ is *not* included, and\n\n- the right endpoint $-7$ is *not* included.\n\nTherefore, the inequality represented by this interval is \n\n$$\n-\\infty <x<-7.\n$$\n\nHowever, since all numbers are greater than negative infinity, it suffices to write \n\n$$\nx<-7.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
